## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world serverless reliability and CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys, conditional writes, DLQ
- Duplicate detection under retries
- End-to-end latency and scale testing
- Local AWS emulation in CI (LocalStack/SAM)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Idea: idempotent Lambda processor sketch
async function handleEvent(e) {
  const id = `${e.key}:${e.version ?? 'latest'}`;
  if (await db.has(id)) return;
  const data = await s3.read(e.bucket, e.key);
  await db.put({ id, data });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test DLQ poison-pill handling? 
- How would you ensure idempotency across regional deployments?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design practical tests for eventual consistency in offline-first scenarios, including merge behavior, conflict resolution policy, and data integrity under CI.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first and eventual consistency
- Merge policies (last-writer-wins, deterministic merges, or CRDTs)
- Conflict scenarios and data integrity checks
- Deterministic test datasets and network partition simulations
- CI integration, test isolation, and seed data management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Jest-like test (pseudo)
describe('offline sync', () => {
  test('merges offline edits on reconnect using last-writer-wins', async () => {
    const server = new MockServer();
    const clientA = new Client(server, { offline: true });

    server.createNote({ id: 'n1', content: 'Hello' });

    // offline edit on client A
    clientA.createNoteOffline({ id: 'n1', content: 'Hello world' });

    // reconnect and sync
    await clientA.sync();

    // verify on server
    expect(server.getNote('n1').content).toBe('Hello world');
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend tests for concurrent offline edits on two devices?
- How would you validate no PII leakage during sync and how would you test rollback on failed sync?

